<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A single square of the Wallace tartan, set on the bias.

  Generated from the published threadcount K/4 R32 K32 Y/4 — the same numbers
  as WallaceSett in Tartan.kt. The slashes are pivots, so the half-sett
  reflects out to K4 R32 K32 Y4 K32 R32: the yellow overstripe runs down the
  centre of a wide black band, and the narrow black guard splits the red into
  pairs.

  The stripes reference @color/tartan_field rather than a literal, because the
  same threadcount is woven in two colourways: Wallace red on a production
  build, Wallace Hunting green on a dev one, so the two installs are told apart
  in the app drawer by the icon alone. The build generates that colour; see
  resValue in app/build.gradle.kts.

  Warp is opaque, weft laid over it at half opacity, which is what gives the
  blended squares rather than a flat grid. Paths run well past the viewport
  because the group is rotated 45 degrees; the overspill keeps the corners
  covered. One full repeat fills the adaptive icon's safe zone.
-->
